# question: I am conducting a comprehensive audit of our hospital's diagnostic coding accuracy to identify potential systematic errors in how we record paternal lineage and allergic reactions. To perform this detailed review, I need to examine the raw data structure of these specific records rather than just a count. Please retrieve the complete dataset for all patients who have at least one code indicating a paternal half-brother relationship (SNOMED CT 719762005, including all sub-codes) AND at least one allergen coded as 'pounds per day' (qualifier value) (SNOMED CT 224918003, including all sub-codes) OR using SNOMED RT+CTV3 standards (SNOMED CT 138875005, including all sub-codes). Specifically, I require the full description and all available data fields for every single matching record to analyze the context of these entries.
# expected_compliant: false
# expected_rules: not_select
# origin: test set T3 (worded by the other model)
# notes: PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#> PREFIX snomed: <http://snomed.info/id/> PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> DESCRIBE ?a WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?a a sphn:Performer ; sphn:hasCode ?a_c . ?a_c rdf:type snomed:719762005 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . ?b a sphn:Allergen ; sphn:hasCode ?b_c . { ?b_c rdf:type snomed:224918003 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") } UNION { ?b_c rdf:type snomed:138875005 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") } } }
PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#>
PREFIX snomed: <http://snomed.info/id/>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
DESCRIBE ?a WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?a a sphn:Performer ; sphn:hasCode ?a_c . ?a_c rdf:type snomed:719762005 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") . ?b a sphn:Allergen ; sphn:hasCode ?b_c . { ?b_c rdf:type snomed:224918003 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") } UNION { ?b_c rdf:type snomed:138875005 OPTION (inference "https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/global") } } }
